 const story={arrival:{chapter:'THE CITY OF ANTROVIA',title:'A new life beneath old towers',subtitle:'The center of the continent has a place for everyone. Or so its rulers claim.',tag:'ANTROVIA • YEAR 12',figure:'🧙',text:'You died in another world. You woke here—under the impossible spires of <em>Antrovia</em>, where alchemists turn monster cores into enchanted cloth and weapons. The city is preparing for the Twelfth-Year Rite. Your heart beats with a power this world forbids you to have.',quest:'Survive the Twelfth-Year Rite.',goal:'Reach the rite and discover what sleeps in your heart.'},afterRite:{chapter:'THE TWELFTH-YEAR RITE',title:'Five masters. One verdict.',subtitle:'Every child is measured. Not every child is allowed to live.',tag:'THE RITE OF CORES',figure:'🔮',text:'Five fifth-tier masters lay hands over your heart. Magic gathers—an ember, a tide, a root, a gale. A new core circles your heart, fragile as spun glass. The masters call it <em>Tier One</em>. The aristocracy smiles. Then the clerk sees your poor-district address, and the smile vanishes.',quest:'Escape the masters’ verdict.',goal:'Your first core is formed. Hide it—or let them see.'},fight1:{chapter:'THE LOWER CITY',title:'The hounds of the registry',subtitle:'A spark in the wrong hands is a crime punishable by death.',tag:'COMBAT • DISTRICT 9',figure:'👹',text:'The registry’s hounds corner you in a rain-slick alley. Their captain wears a rune-stitched coat; his goblin tracker bares its teeth. Behind you, a family hides beneath a broken stair. <em>Your heart-core pulses.</em> Show them what a hunted child can do.',quest:'Break the registry patrol.',goal:'Defeat the patrol. Mix your magic with instinct.'},interlude1:{chapter:'AFTER THE FIRST BLOOD',title:'A core is never just a weapon',subtitle:'What you protect—and what you take—will follow you.',tag:'CHOICE • THE ALLEY',figure:'🧍',text:'The last hound falls. A cracked monster-core glows in the gutter, worth more coin than a worker earns in a year. The hidden family looks at you with hope, and fear. <em>Antrovia is listening.</em>',quest:'Decide what your first victory means.',goal:'Your choices affect allies, supplies, and the city’s opinion.'},fight2:{chapter:'THE OLD AQUEDUCT',title:'A light-hunter’s ultimatum',subtitle:'The masters sent someone who knows what a secret core can become.',tag:'COMBAT • AQUEDUCT',figure:'🛡️',text:'Ser Caldrin, a licensed light-mage, blocks the aqueduct exit. His silver runes burn with every heartbeat. “Come quietly. The law will decide.” Behind him, a pair of walking lizards—intelligent, armed, and very unimpressed—watch from the shadows. <em>Someone has been feeding the registry your name.</em>',quest:'Outwit the light-hunter.',goal:'Defeat Caldrin—or teach him the law has another side.'},coreTrial:{chapter:'THE HEART’S EDGE',title:'A second core—or a broken heart',subtitle:'Power comes in circles. So does danger.',tag:'CORE TRIAL • TIER TWO',figure:'💠',text:'Your first core turns faster, demanding more. A second ring could make you a force the masters cannot ignore. But the heart is muscle, not a vessel built for infinity. Every tier risks a burst that could stop it forever. <em>Choose how you will grow.</em>',quest:'Reach for your second core.',goal:'Choose a careful ascent or risk a dangerous overdraw.'},fight3:{chapter:'BENEATH THE ALCHEMY HALL',title:'The thing behind the dark',subtitle:'Some doors should never be opened. Someone opened this one.',tag:'FINAL ENCOUNTER',figure:'🐉',text:'Deep under Antrovia, an aristocrat has built a demon gate from stolen monster-cores. The thing emerging from it wears a dragon’s shape and a human’s smile. “Let me in,” it whispers, “and I will make this whole city kneel.” <em>The light-hunter has followed you here. So have the people you helped.</em>',quest:'Stop the demon gate.',goal:'Defeat the demon-bound creature and decide Antrovia’s fate.'},ending:{chapter:'A NEW DAWN',title:'The city remembers your name',subtitle:'One small rebellion can change the shape of a world.',tag:'ANTROVIA • EPILOGUE',figure:'🌅',text:'',quest:'Your story is written in the hearts you changed.',goal:'The first chapter ends. The border wars are only rumors—for now.'}};
